 finally  enjoying his workouts and newfound  lifestyle after coming this far and  getting through the hard part once  patinson knew it would be much easier to  just keep up his routine so he'd never  have to go through the hard bit again  but it didn't really play out that way  as soon as the job's not like no as soon  as he wasn't becoming batman every day  he wasn't working out to keep in tough  physical condition anymore either  number eight the people want what they  want when ben affleck signed on to play  the dark knight he knew audiences would  be expecting a certain level of fitness  so in turn he knew to expect putting his  absolute all into his prep both  emotionally and physically seems all  right but the tricky part was keeping  his age in mind those joints gotta stay  intact strength training was key for him  especially since wearing the batman suit  meant he'd be carrying around a casual  extra 70 pounds affleck overachieved  during his prep for batman vs superman  gaining over 30 pounds and looking slick  as can be weighing in with only 7.7 body  fat he was so fit he actually had to  lose about seven pounds before filming  number nine this guy is shockingly good  at losing and gaining weight christian  bale is known for his wild physical  transformations and prepping for the  dark knight was no exception this bulk  up was kind of insane we're talking a  hundred pounds of muscle how did he even  do it working out every single day  focusing on all the different muscle  groups he needed to work on and when it  came to food it was lean protein healthy  fats and carbs all day every day if he  was feeling like a treat low calorie  fruit and a big glass of water could  always do the trick  number 10 we need some hot packs asap  tom hardy was bulking up hard to play  bane not only was he working out every  day he was doing it four times a day  it's no surprise that with that kind of  training he gained a solid 30 pounds of  muscle and mass it wasn't the best of  experiences in the long run though at  the time hardy explained i think you'd  pay the price with any drastic physical  changes the fact that he was in his 40s  played a big part in the difficulty he  really just had to be much more careful  about how intensely his body was  transforming because well it just wasn't  what it used to be and those aches and  clicking joints became a very real  concern  number 11. what a woman batman vs  superman introduced us to the always  impressive gal gadot as wonder woman but  before she graced our screens the  actress took on an intense physical  workout regime and built up her skills  like nobody's business she did the usual  things clean eating intense workouts  cardio marathons but then she leveled up  we're talking jiu jitsu sword fighting  and kung fu combine that with the gallon  of water she was drinking every day and  you've got a recipe for a wonder of a  woman  number 12. sticking to it is the hardest  part but amy adams was ready when the  actress signed on to play lois lane she  knew her co-stars were going to be  working out hard so she joined in on the  fun when she got into the routine she  found herself on a total role and stayed  fit for all the batman movies she was in  putting in extra effort right before  filming would start of course while her  workouts weren't as intense they were  frequent as she found so much benefit  from them it increases the serotonin so  i find i'm a happier person when i work  out more patient for sure if it works  you better work it number 13. it works  but it costs batman vs superman saw  everyone bringing their a game  especially henry cavill suiting up as  superman everyone has their own way of  getting there but for cavill it was  eating the cleanest meals he could find  that is until he said bye bye to a whole  lot of calories closer to the start of  filming the superman diet isn't fun but  it's definitely effective  number 14 consistency is key henry  cavill was working out non-stop building  muscle mass and strength olympic  weightlifting movements were one of the  major contributors to all those gains  calvel didn't just rely on all the work  he'd done once filming started though  over the course of the 120 day shoot the  actor had the elite trainer mark twight  by his side to keep him in tip-top  condition every single day  number 15 from woman to catwoman to  become as agile and sleek as a catwoman  anne hathaway knew she would need some  help it was about being able to do the  stunts and the fighting perfectly she  brought on personal nutritionist jackie  keller to help with her diet it's all  the boring stuff that no one ever wants  to do hathaway was already in pretty  good shape but toning up was key for her  getting into the role she said it  herself it was a complete transformation  complete transformation is right these  actors really tested their limits and  considering the results it was well  worth it  whose workout routine do you think was  the toughest
 

